Z||000004||2M4 Dale||06-17-2000||10:04 AM||||C'Mon guys any engine can be made to run better ! Plus my "DUCK" gets great fuel economy. Add that to new and upgraded suspension pieces and you've got something.<P>Bro, My Duck ran just fine. I've added a Powerstat low temp thermostat, K&N air and oil filters, AC Delco RapidFire plugs and after market "red wires" from the FieroStore. Now it runs great !!! It also has a new ZOOM clutch in it.<P>Plus my suspension is almost all new. New Monroe Sensatracks all around including the steering stabilizer. New factory rubber bushing up front. Prothane cradle bushings and a Ultimate Dogbone. Oh Yeah...New Goodyear Eagles to get what little horsepower I've got onto the road.<P>Future mods include a performance exhaust from the FieroStore and a high output altinator (better for my sound system) and new ignition stuff.<P>LONG LIVE THE DUKE !!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||ggarsk||06-17-2000||10:05 AM||||You can get a Hooker header from Summit. Part #4702,$265.99 plus shipping. and you nedd a reduducer with a O2 hole...part #11046,$53.00. It takes about 3 weeks for the header...special order.||||reg||1
Z||000006||2M4 Dale||06-18-2000||01:01 AM||||ggarsk, have you or anyone else installed the hooker header ? I would definatly be interested in one of those !<P>It would be cool to hang with the V6's a little better. I'm gettin' tired of outdriving those guys. It would be nice if the Duke would do a little more work...lol||||reg||6
Z||000007||Zman302||06-18-2000||01:25 AM||||You will probably have to ask around for the intake from holley.  I have the new holley cat. at my store and there is no listing for the 2.5 intakes anymore.  If you want alittle better mid range call comp cams.  I special ordered on for my 84 and it made quiet the difference from 2500 to 4000 rpm.  If I can find my cam card ill leave you the part #.  I've also seen cams for the 2.5 listed in the wolverine blue racer book and in the federal mogul performance book but they seemed alittle radical.  with the comp cam i am still getting 25-28 mpg in town and about 32 on the highway with a auto.||||reg||1
